    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2BV5qpdtJJy5oTcV7Vn8R9i)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Based on `main`, which already contains #457 (`sp-echo-help`, merged 2026-11-14); this PR extends it.\n- The linting/batch PR being built on #457 uses only `sp-echo-help-set`, which does not change here; the new key and timer apply to it automatically. If it is based on `457-echo-area-help-hints`, a small textual conflict in `sp-interaction.org` is possible.\n- If merged out of order: nothing breaks.\n- After merging: restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`).\n\n## Summary\n\n- **Request:** keep the hints in the echo area for good, or let a key show them again.\n- **Not done: nano's `sit-for` loop.** `(sit-for 30)` blocks the command until a key is pressed or the time passes; it would freeze the BibTeX buffer's commands. Two non-blocking things do the same job instead:\n  - `C-c ?` (`sp-echo-help-show-now`) in any buffer with `sp-echo-help-mode` shows the hints at once, replacing the current message. Without hints it says so.\n  - An idle timer (`sp-echo-help-idle-delay`, default 1.5 s, nil turns it off) shows the hints again when the echo area is empty. One shared timer; it stops when no buffer uses the mode.\n  - Together with the existing re-show after each command, the hints stay there unless a message of a command is showing; that message is never overwritten, and the hints return on idle.\n- Docs (bullet lists): new part \"Keeping the hints visible\" in `sp-interaction.org`; `.el` re-tangled. Two byte-compile warnings of #457 fixed (long docstring line, free variable).\n- Tests (Emacs 29.3 batch): 2 new (show-now, timer start/stop), 6 of 6 pass in `sp-echo-help-test.el`; 15 of 15 in `sp-fetch-inbox-test.el`. No CHANGELOG edit.\n- **Untested by Claude:** the real GUI, whether `C-c ?` is free in your other modes (it is not used in the config; `C-c` stays in CUA's sense of a prefix only without a region), and eldoc or Embark clearing the echo area.\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [ ] Check out: `cd ~/dotfiles; git fetch origin 461-echo-help-show-key; git checkout 461-echo-help-show-key`, restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`)\n- [ ] Unit tests: `cd ~/.config/emacs-modular; emacs -Q --batch -L libraries/modules/base -L tests -l tests/sp-echo-help-test.el -f ert-run-tests-batch-and-exit` → 6 pass\n- [ ] `C-c w b a`: hints show; `C-c ?` shows them again after another message (for example `M-x` then `C-g`)\n- [ ] Wait 2 s with an empty echo area (press `C-g`): the hints come back\n- [ ] `C-c ?` in a normal buffer: \"No key hints for this buffer\", no error\n- [ ] The hints do not overwrite \"Key: ...\" after `C-c C-r`; they return after the idle delay\n- [ ] `(setq sp-echo-help-idle-delay nil)`, restart: no timer, `C-c ?` and the after-command re-show still work\n- [ ] Emacs stays responsive (no blocking) while the hints are shown\n- [ ] Abort or file the article: no hints show in other buffers\n\n<details><summary>Revert after testing</summary>\n\n- Discard local edits: `git -C ~/dotfiles status`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles restore .`.\n- Back to main: `git -C ~/dotfiles switch main`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles pull`; restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`).\n- Optionally delete the test branch: `git -C ~/dotfiles branch -D 461-echo-help-show-key`.\n- Fish shell works for all of the above; no yadm or Stow steps.\n\n</details>\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi9Q97rFzosc4tkLbQe)_",
